WHAT THIS REPLACES
  The eco-6hoxj.68 lane filed `nc4-skewed-predicate.log` as the control for this
  pin, but the perturbation it recorded was the DRAIN's future-time predicate
  (`usableOtelTime`, `packages/collector-cli/src/server.ts`), which reds
  `u_the_drains_future_time_test_is_the_normalizers_own_over_every_boundary` and
  says nothing about the normalizer copy. There was therefore no evidence the
  normalizer-copy pin could fail at all. The correctly-named drain control is
  kept beside this file as `nc-drain-future-time.log`.

WHAT THE PIN IS
  `SPOOL_RULE_TWO_DISCLOSED_CANONICAL_NAMES` is matched against real key
  spellings using `normalizedSpelling` (`scripts/lib/spool-spelling-corpus.ts`),
  a COPY of the ledger's `normalizeFieldName`, which is not exported. Inside
  `r_every_protected_identity_name_is_blanked_or_declared`, `normalizerCopyDisagrees`
  holds the copy to `isProtectedMetadataFieldName`'s verdict over every name in
  the corpus, so the copy cannot drift into declaring more than a person agreed
  to.

PERTURBATION (scripts/lib/spool-spelling-corpus.ts, worktree only)
  -  return field.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, "").toLowerCase();
  +  return field.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, "");
  The copy stops lowercasing. The real normalizer still does, so the two
  disagree on every mixed-case or upper-case spelling in the corpus.

